# Generated from: specs/292-select-review-base-without-interactive-picker-parsing/requirements.md
Feature: Select review base without interactive picker parsing
  Review workers previously depended on a local default branch and terminal-rendered picker text.
  This was fixed by exact local-or-origin ref resolution and a direct review request.

  # --- Remote-Only Default ---

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Remote-only GitHub default branch reviews without a picker
    Given GitHub reports main and only refs/remotes/origin/main exists
    When execute reaches review1 or review2
    Then review starts against origin/main
    And execute does not submit slash-review, parse picker output, or send picker navigation keys
    And terminal width and wrapped branch names cannot change the result

  # --- Local Default Preserved ---

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Existing local default branch remains the review base
    Given GitHub reports main and refs/heads/main exists
    When execute reaches review
    Then review starts against main
    And execute still waits for the review result and handoff before advancing

  # --- Missing Ref Fails Closed ---

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Missing default refs do not trigger a guessed review
    Given GitHub reports a default branch with no matching local or origin ref
    When execute reaches review
    Then execute stops with review_failed before submitting a review prompt

  # --- Successful Review Handoff ---

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: Successful review prompt advances from its handoff without another wait
    Given the single review and finalization prompt exits successfully
    And it writes the canonical artifact-backed handoff
    When execute observes the controller-owned review worker
    Then execute does not wait for a new future working transition
    And the owned review pane advances without a second prompt

  # --- Pasted-Prompt Recovery ---

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: Exactly pasted stalled review receives one Enter
    Given the single review and finalization prompt returns agent_prompt_stalled
    And that exact prompt is visibly pasted with no handoff
    When execute recovers the prompt
    Then execute sends one Enter and observes the artifact-backed handoff
    And execute does not resend the prompt or require working-state detection

  # --- Direct Review Failure ---

  @SCN006 @regression
  Scenario: True direct review failure stops without recovery
    Given the direct review request fails without agent_prompt_stalled
    When execute starts review
    Then execute stops with review_failed
    And execute does not wait for recovery or send keys

  # --- Skipped Detection With Active Worker ---

  @SCN007 @regression
  Scenario: Stalled review with skipped detection completes from its no-findings handoff
    Given the single review and finalization prompt returns agent_prompt_stalled after about 13 seconds
    And detection reports neither the pasted prompt nor a working state
    And the exact owned sibling OMP worker remains registered
    When that worker writes the canonical no-findings artifact and validated handoff
    Then execute advances without a second prompt or future working transition
    And the owned pane closes only after the handoff is accepted

  # --- Findings Evidence ---

  @SCN008 @regression
  Scenario: Single review prompt persists findings before advancing
    Given the controller submits one exact-base host-review and finalization prompt
    When the sibling reviewers report actionable findings
    Then the worker writes the findings-only canonical artifact
    And the passed review handoff names that existing non-empty artifact

  # --- Hard Failure ---

  @SCN009 @regression
  Scenario: Review worker disappearance without evidence fails closed
    Given the review prompt has not produced a valid handoff
    When the exact owned review worker disappears
    Then execute stops with process_lost
    And execute does not advance or guess completion from state text
